Function strings can be bound to a single name for later use.

ESC>To use this feature, type "DEF>",

then the name you want to use for your custom string,

a comma (","),
and the function strings you would like to apply.

There can be an unlimited number of spaces between any of these parameters.

CLRA>And if your custom string does not end with a greater-than sign (">"), one will be added for you.

If you make a file with the extension .def or .defs, you can use BOLD(IMPORT) to import DEFs inside.

BOLD(IMPORT) uses a file path, so if you have scripts inside a folder inside your main folder, the directory structure would be: "./folder1/folder2/".

"../" will move up one directory, changing "./folder1/folder2/" to "./folder1/".

"./" is the path to the current directory.